                <h2>一、素材池需要准备多少条才够用</h2>
<p>冷启动阶段建议准备 <strong>20-30 条原创素材</strong>。低于这个数量，平台算法能学习到的用户反馈样本不足，系统难以找到精准受众，出价成本会偏高。</p>
<p>实际操作中，很多团队只准备 5-8 条素材就急着上线，结果两天内就把所有素材测试完，发现数据表现差却已经没有新素材可用。TikTok 的机器学习需要一定时间收敛，素材池太小会直接导致冷启动失败。</p>
<blockquote>
<p>经验值：首批素材建议 20 条起，后续每周补充 10-15 条新内容，保持素材池持续有新鲜血液。</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>二、素材上传的节奏怎么安排</h2>
<p><strong>第一天上传 30%，第三天再上传 30%，第五天补充剩余 40%</strong>。不要一次性把素材全部塞进去。</p>
<p>这样操作的逻辑是：首批素材上线后 48 小时能看到初步数据，根据跑出的 CPM、CTR、点击率等指标，判断哪类内容方向更有潜力。第二批素材可以有针对性地调整拍摄角度、口播话术或产品展示方式。分批上传还有一个好处——避免账户被系统判定为异常操作。</p>
<p>一次性上传大量素材容易触发 TikTok 的审核机制，轻则延迟审核，重则导致账户进入观察期。</p>
<hr />
<h2>三、不同素材类型怎么搭配</h2>
<p>建议按 <strong>4:3:3 的比例</strong> 安排：</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>40% 真人出镜类</strong>：包括产品测评、使用场景演示、对比实验等。这类素材在 TikTok 的自然流量获取能力最强，用户信任度更高。</li>
<li><strong>30% 产品展示类</strong>：纯商品展示、B-roll 镜头拼接、卖点字幕卡片等。适合跑信息流广告，转化路径短。</li>
<li><strong>30% UGC 风格类</strong>：仿拍、挑战赛形式、用户视角内容。这类素材原生感强，容易获得平台推荐流量。</li>
</ul>
<p>初期不要全上同一类型。某工具类 App 曾测试发现，全上产品演示视频的 CPM 高达 $12，而混搭 UGC 风格素材后整体 CPM 下降到 $7.5，降幅接近 40%。</p>
<hr />
<h2>四、如何判断素材该暂停还是继续跑</h2>
<p><strong>48 小时是判断节点</strong>：</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>指标</th>
<th>暂停标准</th>
<th>继续观察</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>CTR</td>
<td>低于 0.8%</td>
<td>1%-2% 之间</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>CPM</td>
<td>高于 $15 且无转化</td>
<td>$8-$12 之间</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>转化成本</td>
<td>超过目标 CPA 的 2 倍</td>
<td>在 1.2-1.5 倍之间</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>CTR 低于 0.8% 说明素材和受众不匹配，CPM 高但没转化说明流量质量差。这两种情况直接暂停，不要恋战。</p>
<p>数据在 1.2-1.5 倍目标 CPA 之间的素材不要急着停，可能是学习期波动，再给 24 小时观察。</p>
<hr />
<h2>五、预算在素材池里怎么分配</h2>
<p><strong>不要均分预算</strong>。正确做法是：</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>60% 预算集中在头部 2-3 条表现最好的素材</strong></li>
<li><strong>30% 预算给中期测试的素材</strong></li>
<li><strong>10% 预算留给新素材探索</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>很多运营新手会犯的错误是每条素材分 10 块钱，结果全部都跑不出量。冷启动阶段要把钱集中在已经验证方向的头部素材上，用大预算快速积累转化数据，让系统模型尽快学会找目标用户。</p>
<p>新素材的 10% 探索预算也不要省——这是为下一阶段储备素材池的必要投入。</p>
<hr />
<h2>六、素材池如何做持续迭代</h2>
<p>每周做一次<strong>素材复盘</strong>，按数据表现把素材分为三类：</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>保留继续跑</strong> — 转化成本低于目标 CPA 的 80%</li>
<li><strong>优化后再测</strong> — 转化成本在 80%-120% 之间，可以调整封面、口播或受众人群</li>
<li><strong>直接淘汰</strong> — 超过 120% 且 72 小时无改善迹象</li>
</ol>
<p>淘汰掉的素材不要删除，保留在资产库中。有些素材换个投放国家或调低出价后表现会完全不同。</p>
<p>每淘汰 3 条，至少补充 2 条新素材进来。保持素材池总数不低于 20 条，是冷启动期维持账户活力的基本线。</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>快速行动清单</strong>：</p>
<ul>
<li>✅ 首批准备 20 条素材，按 4:3:3 类型搭配</li>
<li>✅ 分三批上传：Day1 / Day3 / Day5</li>
<li>✅ 48 小时看 CTR 和 CPM，决定暂停还是继续</li>
<li>✅ 60% 预算集中给头部 2-3 条素材</li>
<li>✅ 每周复盘，按三类标签管理素材</li>
</ul>
<p>素材池的搭建质量直接决定冷启动的成败。与其花大量时间优化出价和人群定向，不如在素材端多投入——好素材是 TikTok 广告的灵魂。</p>
            </div>
            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>1. How Many Creatives Do You Need in the Pool</h2>
<p>For cold launch, prepare <strong>20-30 original creatives</strong>. Below this threshold, TikTok's algorithm lacks sufficient user feedback data to learn from, making it difficult to identify the right audience and driving up CPC costs.</p>
<p>In practice, many teams rush to launch with only 5-8 creatives, only to exhaust all testing options within two days and find themselves with no new content when performance disappoints. TikTok's machine learning requires time to converge—too small a pool directly leads to cold launch failure.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rule of thumb: Start with at least 20 creatives, then add 10-15 new ones weekly to keep the pool fresh.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>2. What Is the Right Upload Cadence</h2>
<p><strong>Upload 30% on Day 1, another 30% on Day 3, and the remaining 40% on Day 5</strong>. Avoid dumping all creatives at once.</p>
<p>The logic: initial creatives show preliminary data within 48 hours. Based on CPM, CTR, and click-through metrics, you can identify which content directions show promise. The second batch allows you to adjust filming angles, narration, or product presentation based on what you learn.</p>
<p>Staggered uploads also prevent triggering TikTok's system as suspicious account activity. Flooding the system with bulk uploads risks delayed review or even account review periods.</p>
<hr />
<h2>3. How to Mix Different Creative Types</h2>
<p>Follow a <strong>4:3:3 ratio</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>40% Real-person creatives</strong>: Product reviews, use-case demonstrations, comparison tests. These get the strongest organic reach on TikTok and build user trust.</li>
<li><strong>30% Product showcase creatives</strong>: Pure product displays, B-roll montages, benefit-focused text cards. Ideal for feed ads with shorter conversion paths.</li>
<li><strong>30% UGC-style creatives</strong>: Duets, challenge formats, user-perspective content. These feel native and are more likely to get platform recommendation traffic.</li>
</ul>
<p>Don't launch with all creatives from one category. A utility app once tested all product demos—CPM hit $12. After mixing in UGC-style content, overall CPM dropped to $7.5, a nearly 40% improvement.</p>
<hr />
<h2>4. When to Pause vs. Continue a Creative</h2>
<p><strong>48 hours is the judgment point</strong>:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Metric</th>
<th>Pause Criteria</th>
<th>Continue Monitoring</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>CTR</td>
<td>Below 0.8%</td>
<td>Between 1%-2%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>CPM</td>
<td>Above $15 with no conversions</td>
<td>Between $8-$12</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>CPA</td>
<td>Over 2x target CPA</td>
<td>Between 1.2-1.5x target</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Low CTR means creative-audience mismatch. High CPM without conversions signals poor traffic quality. In both cases, pause immediately—don't hold on hope.</p>
<p>Creatives performing at 1.2-1.5x target CPA deserve more time. This could be learning phase fluctuation; give them another 24 hours before deciding.</p>
<hr />
<h2>5. How to Allocate Budget Across the Creative Pool</h2>
<p><strong>Don't split budget evenly</strong>. The correct approach:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>60% of budget concentrated on the top 2-3 performing creatives</strong></li>
<li><strong>30% for mid-phase testing creatives</strong></li>
<li><strong>10% reserved for new creative exploration</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>A common rookie mistake: allocating $10 to every creative, resulting in nothing getting enough volume to test properly. During cold launch, concentrate spend on validated top performers to rapidly accumulate conversion data and help the algorithm learn your target users faster.</p>
<p>Don't skip the 10% exploration budget—this is essential investment in building the next generation of your creative pool.</p>
<hr />
<h2>6. How to Continuously Iterate the Creative Pool</h2>
<p>Conduct a <strong>weekly creative review</strong>, classifying creatives into three tiers:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Keep running</strong> — CPA below 80% of target</li>
<li><strong>Optimize and retest</strong> — CPA between 80%-120% of target; adjust thumbnail, narration, or audience targeting</li>
<li><strong>Retire</strong> — Over 120% of target CPA with no improvement after 72 hours</li>
</ol>
<p>Don't delete retired creatives—archive them. Some creatives perform differently when retargeted to another country or with reduced bids.</p>
<p>For every 3 creatives retired, add at least 2 new ones. Maintaining a pool of at least 20 creatives is the baseline for keeping your account active during cold launch.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Quick Action Checklist</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>✅ Prepare 20 creatives initially, mixed at 4:3:3 ratio</li>
<li>✅ Upload in three batches: Day 1 / Day 3 / Day 5</li>
<li>✅ Check CTR and CPM at 48 hours to decide pause or continue</li>
<li>✅ Concentrate 60% of budget on top 2-3 performers</li>
<li>✅ Weekly review with three-tier creative tagging</li>
</ul>
<p>The quality of your creative pool directly determines cold launch success. Instead of spending excessive time optimizing bids and audience targeting, invest more in content—great creatives are the soul of TikTok advertising.</p>
